#
# Dev environment overrides for scripts/dev.sh. Copy to scripts/dev.env
# (gitignored) and uncomment what you want to change.
#
# All defaults below are deliberately shifted by +10000 from the UAT
# defaults so dev can run alongside a UAT/another service stack on the same
# machine without port collisions. The api default is 3030 specifically
# because port 3000 is owned by another service on the host —
# NEVER use 3000 for dev API or you'll fight over the socket.

# ─── Host port mappings (shifted from UAT defaults) ─────────────────────
# POSTGRES_PORT_DEV=15432
# VALKEY_PORT_DEV=16379

# ─── OSRM (SHARED with UAT — no second container) ───────────────────────
# Running a second OSRM instance OOMs the host (NL-foot extract peaks at
# ~5-6 GiB during preprocessing). Dev points at UAT's already-running
# osrm via host-published port 5000. Read-only HTTP calls — no risk to
# UAT. Override if your UAT runs OSRM on a non-default port.
# OSRM_URL_DEV=http://localhost:5000

# ─── Landuse (ADR-0009) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Dev reads landuse_polygons directly from the dev Postgres (just like
# UAT does from the UAT Postgres). Run the one-shot import once via the
# UAT compose file (or against the dev DB directly) to populate it.
# No env var needed in dev.env — there's no separate landuse service.

# ─── Local processes ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# API_PORT_DEV=3030       # DO NOT set to 3000 (another service on the host)
# WEB_PORT_DEV=5173       # Vite default; safe to keep

# ─── Raw GPX uploads (preserved for /admin/uploads/:id/reprocess) ──────
# Default: $ROOT/data/uploads (gitignored). Override to share a folder
# across multiple checkouts or to push to an external disk.
# UPLOADS_DIR_DEV=/var/lib/gctp/uploads

# ─── Dev DB ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Distinct db name (gctp_dev, not gctp) so a `psql` connection string
# makes the dev-vs-uat distinction visible at a glance.
# POSTGRES_USER_DEV=gctp
# POSTGRES_PASSWORD_DEV=gctp-dev
# POSTGRES_DB_DEV=gctp_dev

# ─── Planner ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# TOUR_PLANNER=greedy
# JWT_SECRET=dev-secret-change-me
# LOG_LEVEL=info
